# haunt

Local-first verbatim memory. Hooks store prompts, replies, and tool calls
automatically (no summarization, no LLM). MCP server name is `lore`;
tools are prefixed `memory_`.

## Every turn

1. At the start of a turn, call `memory_recall` with the user's exact
   wording before acting. If the session just started and worldview
   context is already present, you may skip the redundant recall.
2. After acting, let hooks store the turn automatically. If hooks are
   missing, call `memory_observe` with the verbatim text (tier=episodic
   for chat, tier=semantic for durable facts).
3. Never summarize or distill into memory — pass text as-is.

## Worldview

Call `memory_worldview` when you need the full namespace briefing (facts,
entities, procedure index, counts). The sessionStart hook returns a
compact worldview card automatically.

## Procedures

Use `memory_procedure` (action=write) only when promoting a specific
how-to the user wants remembered — not on every turn. Include a clear
`name`, verbatim `body` (steps), and optional `trigger` (one-liner of
when to invoke it).

## Rules

- Namespace is inferred from the project (`CURSOR_PROJECT_DIR` / git /
  cwd). Do not invent a different namespace unless the user asks.
- Hooks skip MCP tools whose names start with `memory_` — do not
  observe memory tool calls to avoid recursion.
- Home dir is `~/.lore` (`LORE_HOME`, or `ENGRAM_HOME` as alias).
- No API keys required. All storage and retrieval is local SQLite.
